/build/
*.apk
__pycache__/

# The signing key is committed on purpose, and the repository root ignores *.jks. Android
# refuses an update signed with a different key, so a key that changed between builds would
# make every update cost the owner their workspace and their signed-in accounts. This key is
# deliberately public: it proves nothing about origin, it only guarantees the next build
# installs over this one. A Play Store release uses a private key in POCKETAGENT_KEYSTORE.
!.signing/*.jks
